AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::initialize()
├── when called on the implementation contract
│   └── it should revert because initializers are disabled
├── when the proxy is already initialized
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInitialization
├── given invalid credit market parameters
│   ├── when IRM is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when IRM has no code
│   │   └── it should revert during registration and leave the proxy uninitialized
│   ├── when credit account is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when fee recipient is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when borrow token is zero address and differs from collateral token
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when collateral token is zero address and differs from borrow token
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when oracle is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when emergency admin is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoBaseMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when owner is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with OwnableInvalidOwner
│   ├── when credit limit is zero
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when credit limit exceeds uint128 max
│   │   └── it should revert with MathUtilsMaxUint128Overflow during checked conversion
│   ├── when opening fee exceeds MATH_PRECISION
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when max LTV equals foreclosure LTV
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when max LTV exceeds foreclosure LTV
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when foreclosure LTV exceeds MATH_PRECISION
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   └── when IRM rejects market registration
│       └── it should revert atomically and leave the proxy uninitialized
├── given invalid Convex configuration
│   ├── when Booster is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when reward recipient is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when Booster poolInfo reverts or returns malformed data
│   │   └── it should propagate the failure and roll back all initialization
│   ├── when pool LP token is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when pool deposit token is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when pool gauge is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when pool reward pool is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketZeroAddress
│   ├── when pool is shut down
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when pool LP token differs from collateral token
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when reward pool PID differs from configured pool ID
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when reward pool operator differs from Booster
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when reward pool staking token differs from deposit token
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when reward pool PID operator or staking token query reverts or returns malformed data
│   │   └── it should propagate the failure and roll back all initialization
│   ├── when reward token list is empty
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when a reward token is zero address
